[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65747,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiomyofibroblastoma is a benign, well-circumscribed myofibroblastic neoplasm, usually arising in the pelviperineal region, especially the vulva, and apparently composed of stromal cells distinctive to this anatomical region.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65748,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8826/0 Angiomyofibroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65749,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E89.1 &amp; XH8A47 Benign tumours of uncertain differentiation, soft tissue &amp; Angiomyofibroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65750,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65751,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65752,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Virtually all cases arise in pelviperineal subcutaneous tissue, with most arising in the vulva. About 10&ndash;15% of cases are located in the vagina. Lesions in men occur rarely.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65753,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients typically present with a painless mass misinterpreted as a cyst {1314521; 9308729}. Occasional tumours are pedunculated {22371044}. Angiomyofibroblastoma is usually smaller than 5&nbsp;cm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65754,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients are commonly of reproductive age {8685229; 9308729}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65755,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65756,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This neoplasm is thought to derive from the subepithelial mesenchyme of the lower genital tract.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65757,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most tumours are well demarcated and surrounded by a thin pseudocapsule. The cut surface is tan-white and solid {1314521; 7551008; 9308729}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65758,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiomyofibroblastoma has alternating zones of cellularity and prominent small to medium-sized thin-walled vessels in an oedematous matrix {1314521; 7551008; 8685229; 9308729}. Tumour cells often cluster adjacent to blood vessels, and areas with denser vasculature (hypercellular) are juxtaposed with areas of oedematous stroma, sparse blood vessels, and tumour cells (hypocellular). Tumour cells are spindled to ovoid, with a centrally to eccentrically located round nucleus, giving them a plasmacytoid appearance. Binucleated and multinucleated cells can be present. Mitotic activity is infrequent to not identifiable. There is usually some quantity of stromal collagen, either fine fibrils or sclerotic plaques. A mast cell infiltrate is found in many tumours. Intratumoural mature adipocytes can be focal or (in rare examples) nearly diffuse, and they have been reported as a lipomatous pattern {15782077}.</p>\r\n<p>By immunohistochemistry, the majority of cases show strong and diffuse positive staining for desmin, whereas, at most, there is usually only focal positivity for SMA or pan-muscle actin {1314521}. Desmin staining may be reduced or absent in cases in postmenopausal women. Tumour cells are consistently positive for ER and PR and occasionally positive for CD34.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65759,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65760,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65761,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> well-circumscribed tumour; prominent small to medium-sized blood vessels with clustered cytologically bland ovoid to spindled tumour cells; infrequent to absent mitotic figures.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65762,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65763,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is no potential for recurrence. One case associated with sarcomatous transformation locally recurred 2&nbsp;years after initial excision {9298888}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:23:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]